To convert a picture to a mesh in Blender using an MCP (Model Context Protocol) 
server, you need a local tool or plugin that exposes an AI image-to-3D pipeline 
to Blender.Recommended Workflow[Blender] <---> [MCP Client Addon] <---> [MCP Server] 
<---> [AI API / Local Model]
The MCP Server: You run a server (like a Python script) that connects to a 
"Picture to Mesh" AI model. This can be a local model (e.g., TripoSR, SV3D)
or an API service (e.g., Tripo3D, Meshy, CSM).The Blender Client: You use an 
MCP-enabled Blender add-on or Python console script to call the server's 
tools.Step-by-Step Implementation1. Setup the MCP ServerCreate an MCP server
that registers a picture_to_mesh tool. You can use the official Python MCP SDK.
